{
    "id": "objective-empty-ground",
    "title": "A reward only the board explains",
    "why": "`frontier` carries region value 0 — DEFEND doesn't apply (not ours), EXPAND doesn't apply (not neutral), and ATTACK's own gate (`(r.value or 0) > 0`) excludes it too, so nothing in the STANDING slate ever sends a directive there. A control objective posts on it at frame 300 anyway, defended by a token force a massed package can clear. The only way an AI issues a directive on this ground, ever, is by reading the board — this is the isolate the ai-eval report's first run couldn't get from objective-next-door, where the same directive would have fired from the implicit EXPAND goal regardless of the board (docs/reviews/2026-09-10/ai-framework.md 'What the first run found' #3).",
    "frames": 1800,
    "team": 0,
    "player": 7,
    "pool": 60,
